{
  "version": 1,
  "size": 20.0,
  "about": {"title": "Cornrows", "category": "Braids", "description": "Draw the rows from the hairline back (the Draw tool, into the braids group). Each row picks up the hair on either side as it goes (feed), every crossing taking in a band from its own side, the rows parting halfway between them; past feedUntil they leave the head and hang as braids, a bead at each end. region: how far a row reaches (half the gap between rows, or a little more)."},
